  "version": 1,
  "description": "The single reviewed XAU shallow/deep entry-ladder and risk-leg specification, with hand-computed cases. Held identical by the manual /algo plan builder (manual_plan.py), the Auto Algo XAU entry policy (execution_route.py) and the Python calculator (xau_ladder.py). The RISK leg belongs to the planner: risk_leg.py declares it in entry.risk_leg (price and lots from these cases) and the executor (TradePlanRuntime.cs) places exactly the declared leg; its C# parity test pins the lots-to-volume conversion. It applies to XAU multi-leg plans regardless of technical-source provenance. Since 2026-11-06 the XAU entry ladder of both Auto Algo (execution_route.py) and Manual /algo (manual_plan.py) is the 60/20/20 three-price ladder one price unit apart (xau_ladder.price_ladder); ZL-1 (ladder_price_cases below): the three prices are distinct, spread from the shallow edge (the live quote inside the zone) to the far edge, every neighbouring pair at least min_leg_spacing_pips (10 pips = 1.00) apart judged after rounding, and a zone that cannot hold two such prices has no ladder (the Auto path refuses the plan, ladder_geometry_unavailable); this file's 0.8/0.2 shallow/deep cases remain the legacy two-leg geometry (kept for non-XAU manual ladders) and the risk-leg contract.",
